================================================================
RULING ON THE PIN COMMIT (55ae908) — the question put to this round
================================================================
Terra flags 55ae908 as strictly later than the red harness (5f38556) and than
the implementation (4aaf764), and asks whether a tripwire-response commit
needs its own red or is census maintenance. W-062's precedent added such a row
in the SAME commit as its implementation.

RULING — the commit has two halves and they rule differently.

(a) The PINNED_A row in containment.test.ts is CENSUS MAINTENANCE. No new red
    is required. A tripwire-response needs no red of its own when the tripwire
    is a pre-existing assertion whose pinned list is DATA: the red belongs to
    the opus that built the census (W-047 behaviour 4), and the tripwire's
    firing is reproducible on demand rather than something a log has to
    remember. Two conditions, both checked here rather than assumed:
      (i)  the tripwire actually fired — REPRODUCED at 4aaf764: exit 1, three
           FAIL rows, "added: [packages/commands/src/verdict.ts:runVerdict:
           opera#1]". It was not a speculative row.
      (ii) the row is live, not decorative — m6 deletes it and the census
           dies. It bites.
    Both hold, so the row stands as maintenance. This is the general rule I
    am adopting for the class, not a one-off indulgence.

(b) The +23-line "row 11" block in verdict.test.ts is NOT census maintenance.
    It is a new assertion, written after the implementation, with no recorded
    red, for a refusal the brief's behaviour-5 table does not list (rev 3
    removed the opus-id containment row; the surviving containment prose is
    about --from). It does bite (m5), so it is not decorative, and regression
    suite changes are the Censor's own ground (qa lex §2) — so I do not fail
    the opus for it. But it should have been either a behaviour-5 row in
    5f38556 with its own red, or, per W-062, in the same commit as the
    implementation. Splitting it did cost something real: A-8, one commit in
    this branch's history that fails its own suite.

Net: the pin stands. The sequencing is a NOTED process finding (A-8), not a
gate failure, and the general rule in (a) is what I will apply next time.

